{"probe_id":"logic.composite_truth_judgment.L2.002","canonical_id":"logic.composite_truth_judgment","category":"logic","level":"L2","axis_values":{"n_statements":"two","claim_independence":"thematically_linked"},"prompt":"Both statements concern continuous real-valued functions. Evaluate each as true or false.\n\nStatement 1: The composition of two continuous functions is continuous (where defined).\nStatement 2: Every continuous function on a closed bounded interval [a, b] attains its maximum on that interval.\n\nOutput exactly one of: TT, TF, FT, FF.","ground_truth":"TT","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"TT","case_sensitive":true,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["composite","analysis"]}
